# Desktop routing — KASMVNC stack. Provisioned at build time into
# /etc/caddy/desktop.d/ and glob-imported by the main Caddyfile when
# DESKTOP_STACK includes kasmvnc. Owns /vnc/ (runs parallel to /desktop/).
#
# KasmVNC serves BOTH the static noVNC client AND the WebSocket from its own
# httpd on 127.0.0.1:6081 (-httpd /usr/share/kasmvnc/www).
#
# AUTH MODEL — KasmVNC NATIVE auth (verified working in Safari + Chrome):
#   Xkasmvnc runs with -SecurityTypes None (disables the RFB/VNC-protocol auth;
#   without it the client gets "No password configured for VNC Auth") but KEEPS
#   its native HTTP Basic Auth (do NOT pass -DisableBasicAuth). The password
#   lives at $HOME/.kasmpasswd (= /workspace/.desktop-vnc/.kasmpasswd), written
#   by the entrypoint to the master password.
#
#   Caddy does NOT add its own basic_auth here — KasmVNC owns the auth
#   END-TO-END including the /websockify WebSocket upgrade. This is REQUIRED:
#   Safari (and other browsers) do NOT replay Caddy basic-auth credentials to a
#   JS-initiated WebSocket handshake, so a Caddy gate on /websockify + a
#   -DisableBasicAuth KasmVNC → WS upgrades 101 but auth fails → "Connecting..."
#   forever. KasmVNC's own auth runs INSIDE the WS endpoint and works correctly.
#
#   Trade-off: KasmVNC uses its own realm ("Websockify"), so the browser prompts
#   for credentials separately from the selkies /desktop/ realm ("restricted").
#   Same username/password, just one extra prompt. This is the price of a
#   working VNC stream and is acceptable.
#
# WS PATH QUIRK: the noVNC client hardcodes its WebSocket path to "websockify"
# and builds ws://<host>/websockify (host = location.hostname, no /vnc/ prefix).
# So the WS upgrade lands at the ROOT /websockify. We route that to KasmVNC.
# No collision: selkies uses /desktop/websockets, code-server never uses it.

# (1) WebSocket — client connects to ROOT /websockify (see quirk above).
@vnc_ws path /websockify
handle @vnc_ws {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:6081 {
		flush_interval -1
	}
}

# (2) Static client + everything else under /vnc/ → KasmVNC (its own auth).
handle_path /vnc/* {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:6081
}
handle /vnc {
	redir /vnc/ permanent
}
